IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cea-types`
IMPORT `cea-dates`

-- Customs and Excise Act 2018 — GOAL 4: REFUNDS AND APPEALS.
--
--   "Must duty paid in error be refunded; how much is refunded on a
--    provisional Customs value; and by when may a decision be appealed?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2018_4.txt — ss 142, 143,
-- and the appeal periods.

§ `Goal 4 — refunds`

-- s 142 "(1) If the chief executive is satisfied that duty has been paid in
-- error, either of law or of fact, the chief executive must, unless there is
-- good reason not to, refund the duty— (a) at any time within 4 years after
-- the duty has been paid; or (b) at any later time if an application is made
-- within 4 years after the duty has been paid." "Within 4 years after" ends
-- on the 4th anniversary (fork F3), or the next working day if that is not one
-- (Legislation Act 2019, s 55; added after the independent pass).
@ref s 142(1)
@export Whether the chief executive must refund duty paid in error under s 142 of the Customs and Excise Act 2018 (NZ): if it was paid in error of law or fact and there is no good reason not to, when the refund is considered within 4 years after payment or an application was made within those 4 years. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN r IS A `Refund facts`  @desc The payment date, any application date, the date the refund is considered, the error, and any good reason not to refund
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty must be refunded` r IF
        r's `duty paid in error, of law or of fact`
    AND NOT r's `good reason not to refund`
    AND (    r's `refund considered on` AT MOST limit
         OR  (CONSIDER r's `refund applied for on`
              WHEN JUST applied THEN applied AT MOST limit
              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))
    WHERE
        limit MEANS `the last day under s 55 for a period ending on` (`add years` (r's `duty paid on`) 4) `, Matariki days` (r's `refund Matariki days`)

-- s 143 "(2) The chief executive must refund the difference between the duty
-- payable on the final Customs value and the duty paid", where the final
-- value gives lower duty (s 143(1)(d)).
@ref s 143
GIVEN paid IS A NUMBER, final IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund on a provisional Customs value, duty paid` paid `, duty on the final value` final MEANS
    max 0 (paid MINUS final)

-- ss 113(3), 123(4), 124(8), 142(3) and others: "within 20 working days after
-- the date on which notice of the decision is given, appeal to a Customs
-- Appeal Authority".
@ref ss 113(3), 123(4), 124(8), 142(3)
GIVEN notice IS A DATE, matariki IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to appeal a decision notified on` notice `, Matariki days` matariki MEANS
    `the` 20 `th working day after` notice `, Matariki days` matariki
